            {
                "entry_id": "b57be92a-cf4a-3fd2-a9ef-6e352e804b0b",
                "word": "twain",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ee1779b2-9ba0-4132-86ad-13f5f5ec908b",
                        "entry_id": "b57be92a-cf4a-3fd2-a9ef-6e352e804b0b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "twains"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5899577-908e-380d-9939-1fe9d161b318",
                        "entry_id": "b57be92a-cf4a-3fd2-a9ef-6e352e804b0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pair, couple."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddbc8b4f-8afe-417f-8440-8d11f85d2fa9",
                                "sense_id": "e5899577-908e-380d-9939-1fe9d161b318",
                                "text": "The susceptible twain, on the search for adventure, dropped in."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bad44856-5309-47f2-a199-437bca8b3f63",
                                "sense_id": "e5899577-908e-380d-9939-1fe9d161b318",
                                "text": "The twain immediately proffered their companionship.\n‘I will come with you,’ said Mr Lessingham.\n‘And I,’ echoed Sydney."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "de4b3130-687b-3c54-a954-f5442d39197b",
                "word": "twain",
                "pos": "num",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                        "entry_id": "de4b3130-687b-3c54-a954-f5442d39197b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "two"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "94891746-9f55-43de-92af-6df0c30687dc",
                                "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                                "text": "But the warm twilight round us twain will never rise again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3acd6653-3760-479e-a089-b1800412934c",
                                "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                                "text": "Bring me these twain cups of wine and water, and let us drink from the one we feel more befitting of this day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96c0483f-81e0-477d-8736-e0d25c5e6e7d",
                                "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                                "text": "Since I haue your good leaue to goe away,\nI will make haſt; but till I come againe,\nNo bed ſhall ere be guilty of my ſtay,\nNor reſt be interpoſer twixt vs twaine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f75a6b79-a708-40e6-bb6b-c928595660b2",
                                "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                                "text": "A month or twain to live on honeycomb\nIs pleasant;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c7d80d9-4520-4d1a-8e7a-b9db078cddc6",
                                "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                                "text": "Oh, East is East and West is West, and never the twain shall meet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "234d0109-2e37-445c-959f-e2fc02a70137",
                                "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                                "text": "And whenever Sir Chetwynd spoke of his \"young girls\" he was moved to irreverent smiling, as he knew the youngest of the twain was at least thirty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ccba7f7-5aa7-4bde-ac20-2a6f007d7fb0",
                                "sense_id": "0261a7cc-b8c9-35ee-ae2c-176fd9bb3103",
                                "text": "[…] all too soon we twain shall tread\nThe bitter pastures of the dead:\nEstranged, sad spectres of the night."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
